The technology viewer’s Retry cannot reliably recover from a cached, corrupt HTTP 200 image. The authorized two-photos-per-group preload policy is not itself a finding.

Review comment:

- [P2] Bypass a corrupt cached response when retrying a technology photo — /Users/asmirnou/Projects/g/ramsider/components/TechnologyViewer.tsx:240-240
  If a technology photo returns corrupt bytes with HTTP 200 and the browser caches that response, Retry calls `select(requested.current)`, which fetches the same URL again. Removing the failed entry from the in-memory resource map does not clear the browser cache, so the viewer can remain stuck on the error state. Retry needs a fresh cache key or an equivalent cache-bypassing request, as the page-image retry already uses.
